# Repo-wide LF, regardless of core.autocrlf on the machine that checked it out. Without
# this, core.autocrlf=true silently reintroduces CRLF into text files on every checkout,
# stash pop, or reset — found twice in one session: scripts/hooks-local/pre-commit's
# shebang broke ("#!/bin/sh\r", kernel could not exec it), and
# packages/ui/test/db/bundle-drivers-disposition.test.ts failed to parse ("SyntaxError:
# Invalid or unexpected token"). text=auto still lets git skip genuine binaries.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git hooks must stay LF and executable — kept explicit as the historical precedent for
# the rule above; the blanket rule already covers this, but a hook that silently stops
# being exec'd is expensive enough to fail loudly and specifically.
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
scripts/hooks-local/* text eol=lf
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
